  "arrangementNotes": [
    "A larger continuous dramatic arc for the final crossing, with independent string, cello, pad, and bass dynamics.",
    "The opening is deliberately hushed. New inner voices widen the middle register before a brief held suspension clears the way for the principal rise.",
    "D-minor harmony opens gradually upward through the main crescendo; the cello reaches D4 at the crest. No major-mode arrival or rhythmic urgency.",
    "The release settles into E suspended harmony and leaves the responsibility unresolved. Seven distant piano notes recall the opening motif one octave lower.",
    "Expression spans are moderated so the quiet passages remain audible at a background listening level and the long arc survives linear loudness matching."
  ],
